This function is already minimal, so the gain will be small at best. The rewrite makes two changes that do not affect behavior:

- **Branch hint:** `__builtin_expect` marks the common case, where `type` is already set, as the likely path.
- **Single loads:** `type` and `profile` are each read once into locals, so the compiler does not reload member fields.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```